    "body": "(Copy pasted the relevant parts of the commit msg into the sections bellow)\n\nFound this while I was fuzzing the neovim UI with https://github.com/antithesishq/bombadil\n\n## Problem\n\nThe query linter asked for the buffer's parser without naming a language, so it got the parser for the buffer's filetype. That only works while the filetype is query. Once it changes, for example by running `:set ft=python` in the `:EditQuery` buffer, every lint fails with \"Parser could not be created for buffer N and language ...\", raised from the editor's TextChanged and InsertLeave autocommands.\n\n## Solution\n\nThe linter only ever lints query syntax, so it now asks for the query parser explicitly, whatever the buffer's filetype is.",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-15T19:10:09Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
